<!--
  Issue #260: `Token` gained `SecondaryHeading: float option`, the opt-in second rotation channel
  ADR-0102 sanctions. Adding a field to an F# record necessarily changes the arity of its generated
  constructor, so ApiCompat reports CP0002 for the old 16-argument constructor against the published
  0.4.0 baseline. The break is DELIBERATE and recorded — the same shape as `ViewerOptions.LogicalSize`
  (#246) and the `Label` / `AutoLabel` / `LabelMotion` additions before it.

  This file exists because `API compatibility gate` is a REQUIRED status check on `main` (branch
  protection, `enforce_admins` on), so a CP0002 wedges the PR outright. ADR-0101 and the header of
  `scripts/apicompat-check.sh` both still describe the gate as advisory and outside the required set;
  they are out of date, and branch protection is the source of truth. See ADR-0102 § "ApiCompat is a
  required check, whatever ADR-0101 says".

  SCOPE: one diagnostic, one target. `IsBaselineSuppression` confines it to the comparison against the
  published baseline, so a NEW break introduced later still reddens the gate. Do not widen this file to
  silence a break you have not read.

  LIFETIME: delete it once a release carrying this break (>= 0.5.0) is published to the org feed. The
  gate baselines off the feed's latest version, not the repo's, so the suppression is needed only for
  the window between this merge and that publish.
-->
<Suppressions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <Suppression>
    <DiagnosticId>CP0002</DiagnosticId>
    <Target>M:FS.GG.UI.Symbology.Token.#ctor(System.Double,System.Double,System.Double,System.Double,FS.GG.UI.Symbology.Faction,FS.GG.UI.Symbology.Klass,FS.GG.UI.Symbology.Sigil,FS.GG.UI.Symbology.TokenState,System.Double,System.Double,System.Int32,System.Double,System.Boolean,Microsoft.FSharp.Core.FSharpOption{FS.GG.UI.Symbology.LabelText},Microsoft.FSharp.Core.FSharpOption{FS.GG.UI.Symbology.AutoLabelSpec},Microsoft.FSharp.Core.FSharpOption{FS.GG.UI.Symbology.LabelMotion})</Target>
    <Left>lib/net10.0/FS.GG.UI.Symbology.dll</Left>
    <Right>lib/net10.0/FS.GG.UI.Symbology.dll</Right>
    <IsBaselineSuppression>true</IsBaselineSuppression>
  </Suppression>
</Suppressions>